  "pr_number": 5434,
  "issue_number": 5245,
  "issue_title": "fix: /api/submissions/preflight honeypot response doesn't match its declared response schema",
  "issue_body": "## Goal\nFix `/api/submissions/preflight`'s published OpenAPI response contract so it accurately reflects the honeypot short-circuit response, which currently doesn't match its declared `responseSchema`.\n\n## Why this matters\nThe route is registered with `responseSchema: submissionPreflightResponseSchema`, requiring fields like `category`, `slug`, `schema`, `risk`, `expectedNotes`, `blockers`, `warnings`, `duplicates`, `nextAction`, and a `routeSuggestion` enum. But the honeypot path \u2014 a real, intentional, permanent code path (confirmed by `tests/submission-api.test.ts`, \"silently discards honeypot submissions without queueing anything\") \u2014 returns `{ ok: true, valid: false, queued: false }`, which has none of the required fields and includes a `queued` field that isn't in the schema at all. Any API consumer or codegen tool relying on the published OpenAPI contract for this endpoint gets an inaccurate picture of what a real response can look like.\n\n## Current behavior\n`apps/web/src/routes/api/submissions/preflight.ts`:\n```ts\nif (String(payload.honeypot ?? \"\").trim()) {\n  return apiJson({ ok: true, valid: false, queued: false }, ...);\n}\n```\n`submissionPreflightResponseSchema` (`apps/web/src/lib/api/contracts-lib.ts:565-613`) is a union of two variants, both requiring the full field set above, with the non-PR-ready variant `.strict()`.\n\n## Desired behavior\n`submissionPreflightResponseSchema` becomes a union that includes the honeypot response shape as a distinct, documented variant (or the honeypot response is reshaped to satisfy the existing schema without breaking its intentional \"discard silently\" behavior) \u2014 whichever preserves the honeypot's actual security purpose (not revealing to a bot that it was caught) while making the published contract accurate.\n\n## Scope\n- apps/web/src/lib/api/contracts-lib.ts (submissionPreflightResponseSchema)\n- apps/web/src/routes/api/submissions/preflight.ts (only if the response shape itself needs adjusting, not the honeypot logic)\n\n## Out of scope\n- The honeypot detection/discard logic itself (already correct, intentional security behavior \u2014 do not change what triggers it or remove the short-circuit)\n- Any other submission-flow endpoint's contract\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- PR includes `Closes #<issue>`.\n- The published OpenAPI contract for /api/submissions/preflight accurately includes the honeypot response shape as a valid documented response.\n- The honeypot's actual runtime behavior (silent discard, no queueing, no information leak to the caller about being detected) is unchanged.\n- tests/submission-api.test.ts continues to pass unmodified in its honeypot assertion (or is updated only if the response shape itself changes, not the behavior).\n\n## Quality evidence required in the PR\n- No visual impact.\n- List invariants: confirm the honeypot response still gives no signal distinguishing \"caught as a bot\" from other benign early-exit responses, if that's a deliberate security property worth preserving.\n\n## Validation\npnpm exec vitest run tests/submission-api.test.ts tests/api-contracts.test.ts\n",
